### Title

Install a plugin in an installer-protected base.

### Why

An installer can enable plugin installation while protecting base from ordinary package changes. An administrator can freeze plugin installation too.

### Platforms

- [ ] Windows
- [ ] macOS
- [ ] Linux

### Prerequisites

Use a disposable installation built with the new marker and a plugin package available from the installer's channels.

### Steps

1. Activate a different environment. Run `conda plugins install -n base PACKAGE` with the plugin package name.
2. Run `conda plugins list` to see whether the running conda loads the plugin.
3. Create an empty `conda-meta/frozen` file in base. Repeat the install, leaving both markers in place.

### Pass criteria

The first install succeeds without an override and conda lists the plugin. The second install reports that base is frozen.
